Fix heap OOB write in RankFilter via ImagingExpand overflow (CVE-2026-59197)

Pillow before 12.3.0 can trigger a native heap out-of-bounds write when
ImageFilter.RankFilter.filter() calls image.expand(size // 2, size // 2)
with a very large odd filter size before rank-filter size validation.
ImagingExpand() then computes output dimensions with unchecked signed int
arithmetic, wrapping to a tiny allocation while the border-copy loop still
iterates with the huge margin.

This validates oversized filter sizes in RankFilter.__init__() before
expand() is called, and hardens ImagingExpand() against negative margins
and integer overflow in the output dimensions.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/cce3bdb867c77a3420261ed1bfdb6b0787ec8fc1

--- a/src/PIL/ImageFilter.py
+++ b/src/PIL/ImageFilter.py
@@ -77,6 +77,9 @@
     name = "Rank"
 
     def __init__(self, size, rank):
+        if size * size * 4 > (2**31 - 1):
+            msg = "filter size too large"
+            raise ValueError(msg)
         self.size = size
         self.rank = rank
 

--- a/src/libImaging/Filter.c
+++ b/src/libImaging/Filter.c
@@ -54,9 +54,13 @@
     int x, y;
     ImagingSectionCookie cookie;
 
-    if (xmargin < 0 && ymargin < 0) {
+    if (xmargin < 0 || ymargin < 0) {
         return (Imaging)ImagingError_ValueError("bad kernel size");
     }
+    if (xmargin > (INT_MAX - imIn->xsize) / 2 ||
+        ymargin > (INT_MAX - imIn->ysize) / 2) {
+        return (Imaging)ImagingError_ValueError("filter size too large");
+    }
 
     imOut = ImagingNewDirty(
         imIn->mode, imIn->xsize + 2 * xmargin, imIn->ysize + 2 * ymargin);

Bound PdfStream FlateDecode output size (CVE-2026-59200)

Pillow before 12.3.0 calls zlib.decompress() with bufsize set from the PDF
stream Length/DL field. bufsize is only an initial allocation hint, so a
crafted FlateDecode stream can expand far beyond that and exhaust memory.

Use dictionary byte-key access (Filter is str via attribute getattr) plus
zlib.decompressobj() with an explicit max_length (default ImageFile.SAFEBLOCK)
and reject streams that still have unconsumed input.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow/commit/f7a31ea75e460e108c37126da1f47812f21f6b09 (PR #9718)

--- a/src/PIL/PdfParser.py
+++ b/src/PIL/PdfParser.py
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 import zlib
 from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, List, NamedTuple, Union
 
+from . import ImageFile
+
 
 # see 7.9.2.2 Text String Type on page 86 and D.3 PDFDocEncoding Character Set
 # on page 656
@@ -312,19 +314,20 @@
         self.dictionary = dictionary
         self.buf = buf
 
-    def decode(self):
+    def decode(self, max_length=ImageFile.SAFEBLOCK):
         try:
-            filter = self.dictionary.Filter
-        except AttributeError:
+            filter = self.dictionary[b"Filter"]
+        except KeyError:
             return self.buf
         if filter == b"FlateDecode":
-            try:
-                expected_length = self.dictionary.DL
-            except AttributeError:
-                expected_length = self.dictionary.Length
-            return zlib.decompress(self.buf, bufsize=int(expected_length))
+            dobj = zlib.decompressobj()
+            plaintext = dobj.decompress(self.buf, max_length)
+            if dobj.unconsumed_tail:
+                msg = "Decompressed data too large"
+                raise ValueError(msg)
+            return plaintext
         else:
-            msg = f"stream filter {repr(self.dictionary.Filter)} unknown/unsupported"
+            msg = f"stream filter {repr(filter)} unknown/unsupported"
             raise NotImplementedError(msg)
 
 

